        <mxCell id="legend-text" parent="legend" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#17212f;fontSize=16;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;connectable=0;" value="UML notation follows the supplied slides: instance-level nodes (pp. 8-9), nested nodes (p. 12), artifacts (p. 14), deployment specification (p. 16), communication paths (p. 17).&lt;br&gt;Underlined name : Type = node instance; nested artifact = deployed file/directory; solid line = communication path (not a data-flow arrow).&lt;br&gt;Pod names ending in -* identify generated workload instances; actual Pod suffixes were not queried. K3s/Pod/Container are modeled as execution environments.&lt;br&gt;Runtime topology: deploy/production-cloud/k8s-production.py + README.md; gateway routing and Dockerfiles checked. This is a configuration view, not live-cluster verification.&lt;br&gt;Primary gateway / database paths are shown; secondary internal notification calls and external SMTP are omitted. Cloudflare / origin proxy retained from original; live TLS configuration unverified.&lt;br&gt;Production has seven application workloads and three data workloads. Reviews are handled by product-service; no separate review-service is deployed by this profile." vertex="1">
